VALUES
    ($seed$22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000001$seed$, $seed$Senior Accountant$seed$, $seed$Northwind Foods$seed$, $seed$Northwind Foods is a $40M consumer packaged goods business (frozen and shelf-stable snacks sold through grocery and club channels) based in Chicago. We are hiring a Senior Accountant to own the month-end close.

What you will do
- Own the monthly close across three legal entities in NetSuite: journal entries, accruals, prepaids, fixed assets, intercompany eliminations and the consolidated trial balance.
- Prepare balance sheet reconciliations and drive the close from 12 business days down to 7.
- Support trade-spend and broker-commission accruals with the sales finance team.
- Prepare PBC schedules for the annual audit and respond to auditor requests.
- Document close procedures and help train a staff accountant.

What we need
- Active CPA.
- 5+ years of accounting experience with at least 2 years running a month-end close.
- Hands-on NetSuite experience (saved searches, journal imports, multi-subsidiary).
- Strong US GAAP fundamentals, including accruals and fixed-asset accounting.
- Available to work Central time hours; hybrid, 2 days a week in our Chicago office.
- Able to start within two weeks.

Nice to have
- QuickBooks experience (our acquired brand still runs on it during migration).
- CPG or food and beverage industry experience.
- Exposure to trade promotion accounting.$seed$, $seed${"hours_per_week":null,"industries":["consumer_packaged_goods","food_and_beverage"],"min_overlap_hours":null,"min_years_experience":5,"must_haves":["Active CPA","5+ years of accounting experience with at least 2 years running a month-end close","Hands-on NetSuite experience (saved searches, journal imports, multi-subsidiary)","Strong US GAAP fundamentals, including accruals and fixed-asset accounting","Available to work Central time hours; hybrid, 2 days a week in our Chicago office","Able to start within two weeks"],"nice_to_haves":["QuickBooks experience","CPG or food and beverage industry experience","Exposure to trade promotion accounting"],"other_industries":[],"other_preferred_certifications":[],"other_preferred_software":[],"other_required_certifications":[],"other_required_software":[],"preferred_certifications":[],"preferred_software":["quickbooks"],"required_certifications":["cpa_us"],"required_qualifications":[{"accept_equivalents":true,"canonical":"cpa_us","equivalents_stated":false,"name_as_written":"CPA","quote":"Active CPA"}],"required_software":["netsuite"],"timezone":"America/Chicago","title":"Senior Accountant"}$seed$::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('starts_on', (CURRENT_DATE + 7)::text), $seed$["Active CPA","5+ years of accounting experience with at least 2 years running a month-end close","Hands-on NetSuite experience (saved searches, journal imports, multi-subsidiary)","Strong US GAAP fundamentals, including accruals and fixed-asset accounting","Available to work Central time hours; hybrid, 2 days a week in our Chicago office","Able to start within two weeks"]$seed$::jsonb, $seed$["QuickBooks experience","CPG or food and beverage industry experience","Exposure to trade promotion accounting"]$seed$::jsonb, '{cpa_us}', '{netsuite}', 5, $seed$America/Chicago$seed$, 6, 40, CURRENT_DATE + 7, $seed$open$seed$),
    ($seed$22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000002$seed$, $seed$Staff Accountant$seed$, $seed$Brightline Analytics$seed$, $seed$Brightline Analytics is a 60-person Series A SaaS company in San Francisco. This is our first in-house accounting hire; until now the books have been kept by an outsourced firm in QuickBooks Online.

Responsibilities
- Run the day-to-day books in QuickBooks Online: AP through Bill.com, expense reports, customer invoicing and cash application.
- Prepare the monthly close package: bank reconciliations, accruals, prepaid amortisation and deferred revenue schedules.
- Reconcile Stripe payouts to invoices.
- Help the outsourced firm with quarterly sales-tax filings and the year-end 1099 run.
- Take part in our planned move from QuickBooks to NetSuite next year.

Requirements
- 1-4 years of accounting experience, ideally at a startup or a small firm.
- Proficient in QuickBooks Online.
- Comfortable in Excel (lookups, pivots).
- Working knowledge of accrual accounting under US GAAP.
- Based in the Pacific time zone; remote-friendly.

Preferred
- Bill.com and Expensify experience.
- Exposure to ASC 606 or SaaS deferred revenue.
- CPA track.$seed$, $seed${"hours_per_week":null,"industries":["saas"],"min_overlap_hours":null,"min_years_experience":1,"must_haves":["1-4 years of accounting experience, ideally at a startup or a small firm","Proficient in QuickBooks Online","Comfortable in Excel (lookups, pivots)","Working knowledge of accrual accounting under US GAAP","Based in the Pacific time zone; remote-friendly"],"nice_to_haves":["Bill.com and Expensify experience","Exposure to ASC 606 or SaaS deferred revenue","CPA track"],"other_industries":[],"other_preferred_certifications":[],"other_preferred_software":[],"other_required_certifications":[],"other_required_software":[],"preferred_certifications":[],"preferred_software":["bill_com","expensify"],"required_certifications":[],"required_qualifications":[],"required_software":["quickbooks"],"timezone":"America/Los_Angeles","title":"Staff Accountant"}$seed$::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('starts_on', (CURRENT_DATE + 21)::text), $seed$["1-4 years of accounting experience, ideally at a startup or a small firm","Proficient in QuickBooks Online","Comfortable in Excel (lookups, pivots)","Working knowledge of accrual accounting under US GAAP","Based in the Pacific time zone; remote-friendly"]$seed$::jsonb, $seed$["Bill.com and Expensify experience","Exposure to ASC 606 or SaaS deferred revenue","CPA track"]$seed$::jsonb, '{}', '{quickbooks}', 1, $seed$America/Los_Angeles$seed$, 5, 40, CURRENT_DATE + 21, $seed$open$seed$),
    ($seed$22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000003$seed$, $seed$Controller$seed$, $seed$Cascade Precision Manufacturing$seed$, $seed$Cascade Precision Manufacturing machines aerospace and medical components at two plants in Colorado and Utah ($85M revenue, 300 employees, private-equity owned). We are replacing a retiring Controller.

